{"repositoryId":1291067511,"availability":"available","full":"moberghr/beacon","name":"beacon","description":"Semantic database monitoring, alerting, and orchestration for .NET — with a governed MCP server for AI assistants","category":"Developer tools","language":"C#","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-06T13:26:51Z","updated":"2026-10-19T20:51:22Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://moberghr.github.io/beacon","topics":["ai","alerting","data-quality","dotnet","etl","mcp","mcp-server","monitoring","postgresql","sql","sql-server"],"demo":"https://moberghr.github.io/beacon","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T22:20:26.000Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T22:20:26.000Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T22:20:26.000Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T22:20:26.000Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Database monitoring and governed AI access for .NET.","Scheduled SQL checks, alerting and data movement, with an MCP server that gives AI assistants project-scoped, read-only, masked and audited access to your data.","Documentation · Integrate · Quick start · Security model · MCP server"],"features":["Monitoring: multi-step SQL checks run on a cron schedule. Steps can span engines and are joined in memory.","Alerting: results are delivered by email, Microsoft Teams, Slack, Jira or webhook. Tasks are opened when a check fails and resolved when it passes, and statistical anomalies are flagged.","AI access: a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server lets Claude, Cursor, VS Code and other MCP clients explore and query your data through a single governed path.","Data movement: when enabled, audited Insert, Upsert and Truncate-Load jobs write into data sources that an Admin has designated as write targets."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/moberghr/beacon/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"ad5bca5a5c0b141f8b6836a9ce427892cddb4374f250addb8a8bc8b89796cb82","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T22:20